# Per-machine diagnostic output. tools\Diag-WindowsUpdate.ps1 writes .txt transcripts here, which
# *.log above does not catch. This repo is public, and those transcripts carry hostnames, the
# logged-on username, a full hardware/driver inventory and the printer names visible at a property.
logs/
# Exception: this is a reference lookup table (CPU generation -> launch year), not per-machine
# log/audit output. RenamePC.ps1 keeps its own inline copy for actual runtime use (bootstrap.ps1
# doesn't sync research/ to deployed machines) - this committed copy is the source of truth to
# keep that inline copy in sync with by hand. Actual per-machine logs (MachineDetection-Log.csv,
# UnmatchedCPUs.csv) stay gitignored - they contain real BIOS/baseboard serial numbers.
!research/IntelGenYears.csv
